-- title:
--   Uniform bound for twisted orbital integrals at regular diagonal elements
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, and let $\varphi_v \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ be locally constant with compact support. Then there is a real $C \ge 0$ with the following property. Let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ have $\delta_{10} = \delta_{01} = 0$ and $N(\delta_{00}) \ne N(\delta_{11})$, where $N$ denotes the algebra norm of $L \otimes_K K_v$ over $K_v$. Let $\tau'$ be a measure, for the Borel structure of the subspace topology, on the twisted centraliser $\{t : t\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$ (with $\sigma$ acting entrywise on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$), assumed Haar and normalised so that $\tau'$ gives mass $1$ to the part of the maximal compact set of those $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with $g$ and $g^{-1}$ both having entries in the image of the semi-local integers. Let $I \in \mathbb{C}$ be a twisted orbital integral of $\varphi_v$ at $\delta$ relative to $\tau'$, i.e. $I = \int \varphi_v(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x))\,w(x)\,d\mu$ for some twisted section function $w$ attached to $\delta, \tau', \varphi_v$, with $\mu$ the normalised semi-local Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Then $$\|N(\delta_{00}) - N(\delta_{11})\| \cdot \|I\| \le C\,\|N(\delta_{00})N(\delta_{11})\|^{1/2}.$$
--
--   This is the local ingredient, at a finite place $v$ of $K$, for the twisted trace formula of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension $L/K$: the twisted orbital integrals of a fixed test function at regular diagonal twisted classes are bounded after multiplication by the factor $\|N\delta_{00} - N\delta_{11}\|$, uniformly in $\delta$ and in the normalised Haar measure on the twisted centraliser. It is used in the per-class bound [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_lintegral_orbital_doubleCoset_le_mul_prod_rpow_measure`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_lintegral_orbital_doubleCoset_le_mul_prod_rpow_measure).
